================================================================================
Lineage
================================================================================

`slicer-cli` is derived from BambuStudio, which is itself derived from
PrusaSlicer, which is derived from Slic3r. Each layer's contributions are
preserved under AGPLv3.

  Slic3r              — Original FOSS slicer.
                        Copyright (c) 2011 Alessandro Ranellucci and others.
                        https://slic3r.org/
                        AGPLv3.

  PrusaSlicer         — Fork of Slic3r maintained by Prusa Research, with
                        extensive contributions to mesh processing, gcode
                        generation, multi-material handling, and the
                        Arachne wall generator.
                        Copyright (c) 2016 Prusa Research s.r.o.
                        https://github.com/prusa3d/PrusaSlicer
                        AGPLv3.

  BambuStudio         — Fork of PrusaSlicer maintained by Bambu Lab, with
                        contributions to multi-color printing, AMS support,
                        BBL printer profiles, and the slice/preset
                        infrastructure this CLI inherits.
                        Copyright (c) 2022 Bambu Lab Co. Ltd.
                        https://github.com/bambulab/BambuStudio
                        AGPLv3.

  OrcaSlicer          — Fork of BambuStudio/PrusaSlicer maintained by the
                        OrcaSlicer project. The separate Orca CLI binary and
                        profile tree are built from pinned OrcaSlicer source.
                        https://github.com/OrcaSlicer/OrcaSlicer
                        AGPLv3.

  Snapmaker Orca      — Fork of OrcaSlicer maintained by Snapmaker. The
                        Snapmaker CLI binary and profiles use its pinned source.
                        https://github.com/Snapmaker/OrcaSlicer
                        AGPLv3.

`slicer-cli` carries forward this lineage. Modifications made for the
CLI build (CGAL 6.x compatibility patches, Eigen 3.4 SparseMatrix
migration in libigl, Boost ≥ 1.85 compatibility shims, headless
operation) are licensed under AGPLv3 and contributed back where
practical.

