AGPL § 13 — Network use
================================================================================

Users of Helio's hosted slicer functionality can obtain source code, licence
texts and acknowledgements here, without a Helio account:

  https://github.com/Helio-Additive/slicer-cli/blob/main/docs/open-source.md

The page explains how to select the release used by the service and retrieve
its CLI code, pinned engines, override files, patches and build instructions.
The public source repository and releases are:

  https://github.com/Helio-Additive/slicer-cli
  https://github.com/Helio-Additive/slicer-cli/releases

AGPL § 13 requires a modified program to offer its Corresponding Source to
users interacting with it remotely through a computer network. A service
should expose the source link to those users and identify the version it runs.
Subprocess invocation alone is not a basis for claiming an exemption from
that source offer. This notice does not assign a licence to separate plugins
or services; each component retains its applicable terms. See LICENSE and:

